comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T21:30:11.184Z",codex-root,"Hosted evidence: the same high advisory fails both scheduled workflows; the fail-closed behavior is correct and must not be weakened."
  "2026-08-09T21:39:51.583Z",codex-root,"During strict validation, linked-test insertion order exposed a pm-cli 2026.8.9 core hash canonicalization defect. Detailed duplicate search found no matching report; filed upstream issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/955. Reordering tests to the normalized read order restored a clean history-drift result without bypassing the gate."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T21:30:11.184Z",codex-root,Do not suppress or ignore the advisory. Resolve the compatible dependency graph and retain exact strict gates.
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T21:30:11.184Z",codex-root,A release pipeline can be operationally correct yet blocked by newly disclosed toolchain advisories; daily dependency refresh must preserve fail-closed behavior.
  "2026-08-09T21:40:11.323Z",codex-root,"Linked collection ordering must be canonical across mutation, projection, history hashing, and drift validation; otherwise valid metadata can block strict delivery gates."
